        <!-- 56 -->
        <section class="note-card">
            <h2>56. 🌟 Final Takeaway</h2>

            <p>
                Chemical bonding explains how atoms combine and why
                substances have different properties.
            </p>

            <div class="note-card">
                <p>
                    🧂 <strong>Ionic bonding:</strong>
                    attraction between oppositely charged ions.
                </p>

                <p>
                    🤝 <strong>Covalent bonding:</strong>
                    atoms share electron pairs.
                </p>

                <p>
                    🔩 <strong>Metallic bonding:</strong>
                    positive metal ions are attracted to delocalised
                    electrons.
                </p>
            </div>

            <p>
                The most important exam skill is to connect
                <strong>structure → bonding → particles → properties</strong>.
            </p>

            <p>
                Once you can make that connection, questions about melting
                point, electrical conductivity, hardness, solubility and
                physical state become much easier to explain. 🧪⚛️📚
            </p>
